r see a free river to improve to a flush or trips. Since I am leading in the cumulative score, a low-variance play like checking is optimal.\n\nReason:\nThe pot is small and the action has been passive. I have a made hand (Pair of 9s) plus a strong draw (Flush draw). Checking is the best option to realize my equity. It avoids bloating the pot against a potential Ace while keeping the opponent's weaker range in the hand. If the opponent bets, I have easy odds to call given my pair and flush outs.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
